@startuml
' Figure 2.2 – Class diagram: core domain
' 11 of the 24 persisted classes, plus the enumerations they reference.
' Audit columns (created_at, updated_at) are omitted for legibility.
' Behaviour is not shown: the model is relational and operations live in
' the service layer, so the classes carry no methods of their own.
!include ../_style.puml
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 45
hide circle
hide methods

class User {
  - id : UUID
  - accountType : AccountType
  - email : String
  - username : String
  - role : Role
  - plan : Plan
  - earningsBalance : Integer
  - isMarketplaceEligible : Boolean
  - aiTokensRemaining : Integer
  - deletedAt : Timestamp
}
class MagazineProfile {
  - displayName : String
  - slug : String
  - subscriptionStatus : SubscriptionStatus
  - creditBalance : Integer
  - monthlyCreditAllowance : Integer
  - subscriptionExpiresAt : Timestamp
}
class Article {
  - id : UUID
  - title : String
  - slug : String
  - content : Json
  - contentSearch : TsVector
  - status : ArticleStatus
  - placement : Placement
  - visibility : Visibility
  - marketplacePrice : Integer
  - wordCount : Integer
  - publishedAt : Timestamp
  - deletedAt : Timestamp
}
class Tag {
  - name : String
  - slug : String
}
class ArticleTag
class Comment {
  - content : Text
  - deletedAt : Timestamp
}
class Like
class Repost
class Follow
class Notification {
  - type : NotificationType
  - data : Json
  - isRead : Boolean
}
class Report {
  - targetType : ReportTargetType
  - targetId : UUID
  - reason : Text
  - status : ReportStatus
}

class AccountType <<Enumeration>> {
  personal
  magazine
}
class Role <<Enumeration>> {
  reader
  writer
  admin
}
class Plan <<Enumeration>> {
  free
  premium
}
class ArticleStatus <<Enumeration>> {
  draft
  published
}
class Placement <<Enumeration>> {
  public
  marketplace
}
class Visibility <<Enumeration>> {
  free
  premium
}
class NotificationType <<Enumeration>> {
  follow
  like
  comment
  reply
  repost
  article_previewed
  article_purchased
  earnings_credited
  subscription_renewed
}
class ReportTargetType <<Enumeration>> {
  article
  user
  comment
}
class ReportStatus <<Enumeration>> {
  pending
  reviewed
  resolved
  dismissed
}

User "1" -- "0..1" MagazineProfile : extends
User "1" -- "0..*" Article : writes
User "1" -- "0..*" Comment : posts
User "1" -- "0..*" Like : gives
User "1" -- "0..*" Repost : shares
User "1" -- "0..*" Follow : follows
User "1" -- "0..*" Notification : receives
User "0..1" -- "0..*" Report : files
Article "1" -- "0..*" Comment : carries
Article "1" -- "0..*" Like
Article "1" -- "0..*" Repost
Article "1" -- "0..*" ArticleTag
Tag "1" -- "0..*" ArticleTag
Comment "0..1" -- "0..*" Comment : replies to

note as N1
  role and plan are NULL for a magazine account,
  enforced by a CHECK constraint. They are
  orthogonal: a writer may stay on the free plan.
end note

' Keep the enumerations in one column to the side, as the example
' report places them, instead of letting them widen the figure.
AccountType -[hidden]down- Role
Role -[hidden]down- Plan
ArticleStatus -[hidden]down- Placement
Placement -[hidden]down- Visibility
NotificationType -[hidden]down- ReportTargetType
ReportTargetType -[hidden]down- ReportStatus
AccountType -[hidden]right- ArticleStatus
ArticleStatus -[hidden]right- NotificationType
@enduml
